      ":question/id": "1697b167-a282-5f60-b6d4-b5d012306df0",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)=6$?\n\nI. $A\\text{ is not invertible}$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{6}$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 6$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{6} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=6 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\nThe given full rank implies that $A$ is invertible.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)=6$, $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$, $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{6}$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false: $A\\text{ is not invertible}$. $A$ is invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true: $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{6}$. $\\text{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{6}$.\n\n- Statement III is true: $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 6$. $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is II and III only.",
